# Sentinels backend environment
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in the same directory (backend/.env) and fill in
# real values there. `.env` is gitignored — this .env.example file is the one
# that's committed, and it must never contain a real key.

# --- GROQ_API_KEY (optional) ---------------------------------------------
#
# Powers the AI layer's plain-language summary (backend/ai/analyst.py) —
# 2-4 sentences at the top of every report, explaining the findings in
# plain English instead of just a score and a list.
#
# Get a free key at https://console.groq.com/keys (Groq's free tier is
# enough for this project — no paid plan needed).
#
# This is the ONLY thing this key affects. Sentinels is designed to work
# completely without it: leave this blank and every scan still runs all
# five agents and returns a full, correctly scored report — the `summary`
# field is just an empty string instead of AI-written text. Nothing errors,
# nothing degrades elsewhere, and no other feature (including PDF export)
# depends on this key in any way.
GROQ_API_KEY=

# --- SENTINELS_SESSION_SECRET (required for sign-in) --------------------
#
# Signs the session cookie (backend/auth/session.py). Any long random string
# works — e.g. `python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"`.
# Unlike GROQ_API_KEY, this one is NOT optional: every route except /,
# /health, /agents, /repo/agents, and /auth/* requires a signed-in user, and
# without this secret there is no way to tell a real session from a forged
# one, so those routes refuse to serve at all (503) rather than silently
# letting everyone in.
SENTINELS_SESSION_SECRET=

# --- GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_ID / GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_SECRET (required) ---------
#
# From the "Sentinels Autofix" GitHub App's settings page
# (github.com/settings/apps -> your app -> General). These power
# "Sign in with GitHub" (backend/auth/github_oauth.py). Registering the App
# itself, and its repo-write permissions for later stages, is documented in
# docs/PLAN-v5.md — this file only needs the two values below to make sign-in
# work.
GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- SENTINELS_FRONTEND_ORIGIN (optional) --------------------------------
#
# Where the browser is sent after a successful sign-in. Defaults to
# http://localhost:3000, the Next.js dev server's default — only set this if
# your frontend runs somewhere else.
SENTINELS_FRONTEND_ORIGIN=
